   {
    "name": "_check_not_overlapping_regular_skill",
    "kind": "validation",
    "arguments": [
     "self"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "hr_skills",
      "decorators": [
       {
        "name": "api.constrains",
        "arguments": [
         {
          "expression": "lambda self: ['valid_from', 'valid_to', 'skill_id', 'skill_type_id', 'skill_level_id', self._linked_field_name()]"
         }
        ],
        "options": {}
       }
      ],
      "documentation": "The following is the core functionality and difference for the two models\nSkills:\n    1. There can only be one active skill for each skill_id, f.ex only one level of English allowed.\n    2. Skills should not be deleted, unless they were created within the last 24 hours. Skills should instead\n        be archived to preserve the history of the skills linked to that particular record.\n    3. Skills should not be written to, instead the previous skill should be archived and a new skill with\n        the new values should be created. This is again to preserve the history of skills on the record.\nCertifications:\n    1. There can be many certifications with the same skill_id and skill_level as long as the valid_from and\n        valid_to fields are different, e.g. \"the system:Certified 2025-1-1 to 2025-12-31\" can exist alongside\n        \"the system:Certified 2024-6-1 to 2025-5-31\".\n    2. Certifications can be deleted at any point.\n    3. Certifications should not be written to, instead the previous certification should be archived and a new\n        certification with the new values should be created.\nFor both models:\n    1. There should not be multiple records with exactly the same values.\n    2. An Active skill/certification is one with the valid_to field either unset or set to a date in the future",
      "size_in_lines": 42,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": [
